  "details": "# Issue:\n\nFlipping the camera to the front and then switching between portrait and landscape will always flip the camera back to default (the back).\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Start VRChat in desktop mode and open the camera\n\n2. Flip the camera to the front\n\n3. Switch to portrait\n\nDoing so will not only switch to portrait, but also flip the camera to the back.\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nIf you were also using Full or Semi Auto Focus you will have to tap the screen again, after the camera got flipped from switching between portrait / landscape, to get the focus to be right. \n\nThis seems to happen due to the bug apparently not setting the focus again once it flips.\n\n# Expected Behaviour:\n\nSwitching between portrait and landscape should not flip the camera.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/2b7sr3.mp4",
